<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kazys Grinius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a>–<a href="/years/1950">1950</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kazys Grinius was a Lithuanian physician and politician of the Peasant Populist Union who served as the third President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> in 1926. Elected after the left-wing parties won that year's parliamentary election, he was removed within months by the military coup of December 1926, which brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antanas-smetona">Antanas Smetona</a> back to power and ended the parliamentary era of the interwar republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kazys-grinius.jpg" alt="Kazys Grinius" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown (added by arz) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kazys_Grinius.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
